WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.556 --> 00:00:18.440
"I don't understand why he's a tailor," Scrooge said, watching Dick Wilkins return to his stitching.

2
00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:22.001
"Wilkins was no great business genius.

3
00:00:23.122 --> 00:00:26.182
But he worked hard and he had me as an example.

4
00:00:27.983 --> 00:00:31.604
He could have had a career in business and made a lot more money."

5
00:00:33.372 --> 00:00:39.838
"I suppose so," the Ghost of Christmas Present said "We must go.

6
00:00:39.858 --> 00:00:43.041
My time grows short, and we have more to see."

7
00:00:45.863 --> 00:00:50.127
Abruptly Scrooge found himself standing in front of an unfamiliar house.

8
00:00:52.089 --> 00:00:55.732
It was a humble place, smaller and shabbier even than Fred's.

9
00:00:57.614 --> 00:00:58.574
"Where are we?"

10
00:00:59.235 --> 00:01:00.116
Scrooge asked.

11
00:01:01.188 --> 00:01:03.509
"I don't recognize this place at all."

12
00:01:03.529 --> 00:01:09.212
"You will recognize the people who live here," the spirit replied.

13
00:01:11.914 --> 00:01:13.595
They drifted in through the wall.

14
00:01:15.836 --> 00:01:19.738
Inside was a woman wearing a dress that had been patched many times.

15
00:01:20.979 --> 00:01:25.061
She'd decorated it with new ribbons, probably to make it look more festive.

16
00:01:26.141 --> 00:01:30.724
Her daughter named Belinda was helping her mash potatoes in a rough wooden bowl.

17
00:01:32.552 --> 00:01:37.656
Nearby, a boy called Peter was laying out battered plates and forks on the table.

18
00:01:37.676 --> 00:01:40.899
"Who are these people?"

19
00:01:41.319 --> 00:01:42.220
Scrooge asked.

20
00:01:43.161 --> 00:01:44.362
"You said I would know them."

21
00:01:46.584 --> 00:01:48.925
Suddenly the door flew open.

22
00:01:50.006 --> 00:01:53.049
A young boy and girl raced in with snow in their hair.

23
00:01:53.069 --> 00:01:55.951
"You're back, Sam and Sarah!"

24
00:01:56.291 --> 00:01:56.992
Peter said.

25
00:01:57.012 --> 00:01:59.514
"The church bells are ringing!"

26
00:01:59.954 --> 00:02:00.735
Sam cried.

27
00:02:00.755 --> 00:02:05.046
"Yes, Father and Tiny Tim will be home soon," Sarah said.

28
00:02:05.066 --> 00:02:07.027
"Tiny Tim?"

29
00:02:07.587 --> 00:02:08.288
Scrooge said.

30
00:02:08.308 --> 00:02:12.870
"Oh! This must be Bob Cratchit's house."

31
00:02:14.091 --> 00:02:17.793
He looked at his companion for confirmation, but none was provided.

32
00:02:19.014 --> 00:02:22.335
The spirit was watching a young woman hurry in after the children.

33
00:02:23.516 --> 00:02:26.318
She was hardly out of her teens, with rosy cheeks.

34
00:02:26.338 --> 00:02:30.400
"Merry Christmas, Mother," she called happily.

35
00:02:31.592 --> 00:02:34.493
The woman dropped her fork and rushed to embrace her daughter.

36
00:02:34.513 --> 00:02:37.274
"Martha, my dear!

37
00:02:37.635 --> 00:02:39.015
I'm so happy you could come."

38
00:02:39.035 --> 00:02:42.276
"I wouldn't want to be anywhere else for Christmas."

39
00:02:43.457 --> 00:02:44.777
Martha hugged her tightly.

40
00:02:46.418 --> 00:02:48.199
Then she hugged Belinda and Peter.

41
00:02:48.219 --> 00:02:50.300
"You've both grown so tall!"

42
00:02:52.541 --> 00:02:54.181
Sam peeked out the front window.

43
00:02:54.201 --> 00:02:58.423
"Here come Father and Tiny Tim.

44
00:02:59.283 --> 00:03:01.144
Quick, Martha—hide!

45
00:03:01.164 --> 00:03:02.085
You can surprise them!"

46
00:03:02.105 --> 00:03:04.426
"Hide, Martha, hide!"

47
00:03:04.906 --> 00:03:06.047
Sarah said excitedly.

48
00:03:07.228 --> 00:03:12.991
The two younger children hurried Martha behind the coat rack while Peter and Belinda looked on with amusement.

49
00:03:14.211 --> 00:03:18.094
A moment later the door opened again to reveal Bob Cratchit.

50
00:03:19.274 --> 00:03:24.017
Tiny Tim was perched upon his shoulder, clutching his little wooden crutch as usual.

51
00:03:24.037 --> 00:03:27.219
"Merry Christmas, family!"

52
00:03:28.379 --> 00:03:29.380
Cratchit looked around.

53
00:03:32.484 --> 00:03:34.385
"Oh dear, where's our Martha?

54
00:03:35.026 --> 00:03:36.446
I thought she'd be here by now."

55
00:03:38.167 --> 00:03:39.388
Sam stifled a giggle.

56
00:03:41.529 --> 00:03:43.350
But then Martha stepped into view.

57
00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:46.592
"I can't stand to tease you, Father.

58
00:03:46.932 --> 00:03:47.532
Here I am!"

59
00:03:48.993 --> 00:03:53.876
Her father swung Tiny Tim to the ground, holding him steady while the boy got his crutch in

60
00:03:53.936 --> 00:03:57.038
place. Then he hugged Martha tightly.

61
00:03:57.478 --> 00:04:02.697
"We're all here together," he said with a wide smile.

62
00:04:02.717 --> 00:04:05.799
"Now it feels like Christmas!"

63
00:04:05.819 --> 00:04:10.402
"The goose is almost ready, Tiny Tim," Belinda said.

64
00:04:10.422 --> 00:04:12.504
"Come and see!"

65
00:04:14.625 --> 00:04:18.488
Tim hobbled off after her, using his crutch to help himself along.

66
00:04:19.608 --> 00:04:21.149
Mrs. Cratchit watched him go.

67
00:04:21.169 --> 00:04:25.112
"And how was our little Tim?"

68
00:04:25.592 --> 00:04:27.073
she asked her husband quietly.

69
00:04:27.093 --> 00:04:30.636
"As good as gold," Cratchit said.

70
00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:36.562
"He never seems to mind that he can't do all of the things that other children do.

71
00:04:37.982 --> 00:04:42.464
He's happy watching the skaters, though he did ask about skating one day."

72
00:04:43.985 --> 00:04:45.886
Mrs. Cratchit took her husband's hand.

73
00:04:45.906 --> 00:04:48.867
"I'm happy just to have him still with us."

74
00:04:49.887 --> 00:04:51.488
Her voice was nearly a whisper.

75
00:04:52.949 --> 00:04:56.790
Then she cleared her throat and spoke loudly so that the children could hear her.

76
00:04:56.810 --> 00:05:01.192
"Now that your father's home, let's eat before the food gets cold!"

77
00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:07.492
The whole family sat down to enjoy the meal.

78
00:05:08.713 --> 00:05:13.496
Scrooge couldn't help observing that it was much more modest than the meals he'd seen elsewhere.

79
00:05:14.897 --> 00:05:17.719
The goose was so small, it looked more like a duck.

80
00:05:18.779 --> 00:05:22.042
There was hardly enough applesauce and mashed potatoes to go around.

81
00:05:23.783 --> 00:05:25.704
But the family didn't seem to notice.

82
00:05:25.724 --> 00:05:31.388
"There was never a better goose than this one!"

83
00:05:31.712 --> 00:05:32.352
Bob said.

84
00:05:32.372 --> 00:05:36.253
"I've never tasted anything so flavorful."

85
00:05:36.273 --> 00:05:41.535
"Me neither," Peter said, helping himself to another piece.

86
00:05:45.176 --> 00:05:47.476
the potatoes are the best you've ever made, Mother!"

87
00:05:47.876 --> 00:05:48.597
Belinda said.

88
00:05:49.577 --> 00:05:50.837
Mrs. Cratchit beamed.

89
00:05:50.857 --> 00:05:53.958
"I was afraid I might have used too much salt."

90
00:05:55.258 --> 00:05:56.939
"Not at all," Martha said.

91
00:05:56.959 --> 00:05:58.999
"Everything is perfect."

92
00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:01.080
Bob smiled.

93
00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:04.782
"A Merry Christmas to us all, my dears."

94
00:06:04.802 --> 00:06:08.566
"Merry Christmas!"

95
00:06:09.126 --> 00:06:10.447
the family said together.

96
00:06:11.448 --> 00:06:13.049
Tiny Tim chimed in too.

97
00:06:13.069 --> 00:06:15.772
"God bless us, everyone."
